on of services</article-title><source>Am J Public Health</source><year>1995</year><volume>85</volume><fpage>1350</fpage><lpage>1351</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7573615</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Reinhardt</surname><given-names>UE</given-names></name><name><surname>Hussey</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Anderson</surname><given-names>GF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cross-national comparisons of health systems using OECD Data, 1999</article-title><source>Health Affairs</source><year>2002</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>169</fpage><lpage>178</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12025981</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1377/hlthaff.21.3.169</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Elola</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Health care system reforms in western European countries: the relevance of health care organization</article-title><source>Int J Health Serv</source><year>1996</year><volume>26</volume><fpage>239</fpage><lpage>251</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9132374</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2190/TC9K-VQBR-NR64-AGVQ</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Figueras</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Saltman</surname><given-names>RB</given-names></name><name><surname>Busse</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Dubois</surname><given-names>HFW</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Saltman RB, Busse R and Figueras J</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Patterns and performance in social health insurance systems</article-title><source>Social health insurance systems in western Europe</sour